# Normain — Leyton follow-up answers

Period assessed: Jul 2025 – Apr 2026. Drafted 2026-05-08.

## 1. Timeline and expected progression

- **Q3 2025** — RAG product in production; structured weekly evaluation against expected outputs shows quality is insufficient.
- **Oct–Nov 2025** — Decision to abandon RAG.
- **Dec 2025** — Agentic architecture becomes feasible (LLM tool-use maturity + internal experiments).
- **Dec 2025 – 10 Feb 2026** — Full rebuild: 9-tool agentic loop, virtual filesystem (content-addressable, symlinked, ripgrep-backed), cell-by-cell generation, new UI. Launched 10 Feb.
- **Feb 2026 – now** — Post-launch hardening at ~50–220 PRs/month. Active Linear projects: Stability & Quality, Improved source references, Run comparison, Document framework 1.x.
- **Next 6–12 months — primary R&D directions:**
  - Trust and accuracy — narrative reasoning, review-mode integration, PDF-page-accurate citations, output verifiability across arbitrary input formats.
  - World-class chat that behaves as a working colleague, not a query box.
  - Generating and reviewing Word and PowerPoint deliverables in-platform and via plugins for the host applications.
  - Automated workflows that compose Normain's atomic capabilities (extraction, search, calculation, citation, document generation) into multi-step pipelines.
  - Generative UI for white-labelled deployments — letting partners assemble their own Normain-backed apps.
  - Continued: audit-volume scale (100+ docs), reliable subdomain crawling, closed-loop eval harness, tool-set expansion.
- No feature freeze planned.

**Confidence: High.** Phases, dates and active workstreams verifiable from Drive, git log and Linear. Forward roadmap reflects current strategic direction; ordering may shift.

## 2. Uncertainties — evolving and unresolved

**Resolved**
- Agentic loop > RAG for structured knowledge work.
- Virtual filesystem (CAS + symlinks + ripgrep) usable while reorganising mid-indexing.
- Cell-by-cell generation cost-tractable in production.

**Reduced, not closed**
- Trust/verifiability UX — narrative reasoning and review mode shipped; raw tool-call trace still considered insufficient for non-technical reviewers.
- API-throughput stability under load (recurring fixes, not one-shot).

**Still open**
- PDF page-level citation accuracy across multi-column / reflowed / OCR'd inputs — dominant trust blocker.
- Subdomain web crawling (JS rendering, auth, dedup) — generic solution unsolved.
- Speed and scale at audit volumes (100+ docs concurrent).
- Closed-loop eval harness — no canonical metric for agentic structured extraction; metric design is itself a research problem.
- Validation mode integration into the main edit flow.
- Tool-set scope — every new dataset surfaces tool gaps.
- **Chat-as-colleague behaviour** — when an agentic chat should ask, act, defer, refuse, or proactively raise issues. No published model for this; behavioural quality is empirical.
- **Generated Word/PowerPoint quality** — agentic generation, structured review and round-trip editing of binary office formats (and via host-app plugins) is unsolved beyond shallow templating.
- **Workflow orchestration correctness** — composing atomic capabilities into multi-step pipelines while preserving citations, error semantics and re-runnability.
- **Generative UI for white-labelled apps** — letting non-engineers describe a configuration and get a safe, branded, working Normain surface; the design space (capability gating, layout generation, validation) is open.

**Confidence: High.** Categories trace directly to codebase, Leyton checklist and current strategic direction.

## 3. Where experimental effort sits today and is heading

Work where the right approach is not known in advance and is iterated against real-world data:

| Area | Share | Why R&D |
|---|---|---|
| Trust UX + source-reference accuracy | ~30% (continuing focus) | No published solution gives audit-grade citations from agentic extraction over arbitrary inputs. |
| Agent loop quality + tool design | ~20% | New datasets keep surfacing new failure modes; tool-set evolves empirically. |
| Speed/scale at audit volumes | ~10% | Concurrency, batching, model routing, queue stability — tuned per use case. |
| Web ingestion at scale | ~5% | Subdomain crawling, JS rendering, auth — no off-the-shelf solution. |
| Eval/regression infrastructure | ~10% | Metric for agentic structured extraction is a research problem. |
| Chat-as-colleague | ~10% (ramping) | Agent behaviour and turn-taking design with no canonical reference. |
| Word/PowerPoint generation + plugins | ~5% (ramping) | Agentic generation and structured review of binary office formats; plugin surface is novel. |
| Workflow orchestration | ~5% (ramping) | Composing agentic atoms with preserved citations and re-runnability. |
| Generative UI / white-label | ~5% (ramping) | Capability-gated, validated UI synthesis for partner deployments. |

Trust and accuracy remain the largest standing investment; the four ramping areas grow alongside it rather than displacing it.

Excluded as non-R&D: routine UI polish, Vanta dep bumps, Azure infra, ISO/SOC compliance.

**Confidence: High thematic, medium percentages** — categories from recent commits, Linear and stated forward direction; percentages are estimates, not tracked hours. The four ramping areas are growing investments; their share is expected to increase over the next 6–12 months alongside continued trust/accuracy work.

